  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-12-03T09:30:17.520Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "As the title says, there should be more settings for fine-tuning performance/VRAM usage. Some users struggle with VRAM usage because there aren't enough performance settings available. \n\nQualitySettings.anisotropicFiltering - https://docs.unity3d.com/2019.4/Documentation/ScriptReference/QualitySettings-anisotropicFiltering.html\n\nQualitySettings.shadows - https://docs.unity3d.com/2019.4/Documentation/ScriptReference/QualitySettings-shadows.html\n\nQualitySettings.pixelLightCount - https://docs.unity3d.com/2019.4/Documentation/ScriptReference/QualitySettings-pixelLightCount.html\n\nQualitySettings.masterTextureLimit - https://docs.unity3d.com/2019.4/Documentation/ScriptReference/QualitySettings-masterTextureLimit.html\n\nEspecially with masterTextureLimit, you can reduce VRAM usage considerably. It shouldn't be hard to add. You can set it via set_masterTextureLimit. There's a similar feature for mirrors (which might collide with it).",
